From dc92ff63f0582ee985cd74a5927e779f0d69304b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bedirhan=20Gen=C3=A7aslan?=
 <b2210356065@cs.hacettepe.edu.tr>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 17:25:16 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 18/71] Show the cached share of session input on the status
 card
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The card reported input as `non_cached_input()`, the figure the bill is
computed from, but named it plainly `input`. That is the right number to
charge against and the wrong number to reason about: the tokens served from
a warm prompt cache were subtracted and then never mentioned anywhere in the
UI, so a user watching costs had no way to tell whether caching was working
at all.

The counts keep their billing semantics — only the share that was already
invisible becomes visible, as a percentage appended inside the existing dim
parentheses. It is measured over the session total rather than the last
turn, since that is the window the invoice follows, and it is omitted
entirely when nothing was cached, matching how `TokenUsage`'s own `Display`
guards its `(+ N cached)` suffix.

`status_card_token_usage_excludes_cached_tokens` asserted that the word
"cached" appeared nowhere on the card, which was a proxy for its real
subject: that cached tokens are excluded from the reported counts. It now
asserts that directly.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
